    "statement": "The 'absolute SSA degrades EARLIER than the ranking' headline does NOT survive on additive evidence alone. It rested on the covariance-smoothing family (at +0.25 x var: 21.7% median value error while Spearman was still +0.855 of an exact-score +0.878), which is excluded from this presentation. Under the additive frozen field the two degrade in step, and at the strongest level the ranking actually degrades slightly more than the value (12.3% median value error vs 15.6% ranking loss at alpha=2.0). What additive evidence does support is a tail statement: at alpha=2 x s0 the upper decile of cells moves by 29.0% even though the ranking retains 84% of its exact-score Spearman, so individual reported SSA magnitudes can shift materially in a minority of cases where the ordering still looks intact."
